   "": {
    "actClause": "AN ACT to amend the education law, in relation to the issuance of certificate\nof residence forms to individuals desiring to enroll in community colleges as\nnon-resident students",
    "basePrintNo": "S8734",
    "basePrintNoStr": "S8734-2019",
    "coSponsors": {
     "items": [],
     "size": 0
    },
    "fullText": "",
    "fullTextFormats": [],
    "fullTextHtml": "",
    "fullTextTemplate": "",
    "lawCode": "Amd §6222, Ed L",
    "lawSection": "Education Law",
    "memo": "\n \nBILL NUMBER: S8734\n\nSPONSOR: STAVISKY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the education law, in relation to the issuance of\ncertificate of residence forms to individuals desiring to enroll in\ncommunity colleges as non-resident students\n\n \nPURPOSE OR GENERAL IDEA OF BILL:\n\nThe purpose of this bill is to clarify the certificate of residence\nappeals process for persons seeking to enroll in CUNY community\ncolleges.\n\n \nSUMMARY OF SPECIFIC PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1: Section 6222 of the education law is amended to provide a\nprocess for persons to appeal to the Chancellor of the City University\nof New York on a determination for a certificate of residence.\n\nSection 2: Effective date.\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nRecently, SUNY has received appeals on county residency determinations\nfrom persons seeking to enroll in CUNY community colleges. This legis-\nlation would clarify that appeals on certificate of residence determi-\nnations may be made to the chancellor of CUNY.\n\n \nPRIOR LEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nNew Bill.\n\n \nFISCAL IMPLICATIONS:\n\nTo be determined.\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
